grund integrations — print or install the clickable-citation terminal/editor integrations.

Usage:  grund integrations [<client>] [--write] [--conversation plain|link]
                          [--conversation-target file|path|web|vscode|vscodium|cursor] [--format text|json]

With no client, detects the terminal/editor from the environment and prints
what applies. With a client — codium, iterm2, kitty, tmux, vscode, or
wezterm — prints that integration's snippet and the grund-open resolver;
--write installs it as a managed, idempotent block instead of printing. A
write also records the local conversation preference and updates global agent
instructions. With no client, --write with either conversation flag changes
only that preference. --conversation-target picks how a linked citation
addresses its declaration. --format json emits a plan.

Preview and install examples:
  grund integrations                    # detect and list what applies
  grund integrations wezterm            # print the snippet + resolver
  grund integrations wezterm --write    # install it, idempotently
  grund integrations --write --conversation link  # preference only
  grund integrations --write --conversation-target vscodium  # open in the editor

Exit:  0 printed or installed · 2 invalid options, missing write target, or a newer block.
